# DESIGN.md — {name}

> Generated by `di init` on {generatedAt}. Edit freely; keep keys stable for tooling.

product: {name}
category: {category}            # one of the 14 playbooks (skill/categories)
audience: {audience}
stage: {stage}
personality: {personality}      # 2–3 identity adjectives
tokens: {preset}                # theme preset id (skill/tokens/presets)
type: {type}
journey: {journey}
signatures: {signatures}        # the 1–2 screenshottable moves this product owns
voice: {voice}                  # writing rules for UI copy
do_not: {do_not}                # forbidden patterns for this product

# core-kit — React + Tailwind v4 + shadcn/Radix

Base component recipes on host primitives — the skill styles, never replaces. ✅ Deps only: `react`, `tailwindcss` v4 (Radix packages are shadcn-standard, already present). Tokens come from `skill/tokens/` (`di tokens emit --stack tailwind`) as CSS vars.

## 1. Token bridge (paste once in `globals.css`)

Tailwind v4 consumes CSS vars directly; `@theme inline` keeps utilities live-updating on theme flip.

```css
@import "tailwindcss";
:root {
  --bg-base: oklch(0.985 0.004 265); --bg-surface: oklch(1 0.004 265); --bg-elevated: oklch(0.97 0.004 265);
  --bg-overlay: oklch(0.99 0.004 265); --bg-sunken: oklch(0.965 0.004 265);
  --bg-hover: rgba(0,0,0,0.05); --bg-active: rgba(0,0,0,0.08);
  --border-subtle: rgba(0,0,0,0.06); --border-default: rgba(0,0,0,0.10); --border-emphasis: rgba(0,0,0,0.16);
  --text-primary: oklch(0.2 0.01 265); --text-secondary: oklch(0.45 0.01 265); --text-muted: oklch(0.6 0.005 265);
  --accent: oklch(0.605 0.147 278); --accent-hover: oklch(0.565 0.147 278); --accent-active: oklch(0.52 0.145 278);
  --accent-subtle: rgba(111,118,216,0.10);
  --status-info-bg: oklch(0.35 0.11 258 / 0.16); --status-info-text: oklch(0.76 0.1 258); --status-info-border: oklch(0.72 0.12 258 / 0.35);
  --status-success-bg: oklch(0.35 0.1 150 / 0.18); --status-success-text: oklch(0.78 0.15 150); --status-success-border: oklch(0.75 0.14 150 / 0.35);
  --status-warning-bg: oklch(0.35 0.12 82 / 0.18); --status-warning-text: oklch(0.8 0.14 82); --status-warning-border: oklch(0.78 0.14 82 / 0.35);
  --status-danger-bg: oklch(0.33 0.13 27 / 0.18); --status-danger-text: oklch(0.74 0.16 27); --status-danger-border: oklch(0.68 0.17 27 / 0.35);
  --type-body: 14px; --type-small: 13px; --type-display: 20px; --type-mono: 12.5px;
  --radius-sm: 4px; --radius-md: 6px; --radius-lg: 10px; --radius-pill: 999px;
  --motion-fast: 80ms; --motion-base: 160ms;
  --motion-enter: cubic-bezier(0.05, 0.7, 0.1, 1); --motion-exit: cubic-bezier(0.3, 0, 1, 1);
}
[data-theme="dark"] { /* same names, dark values — copy from skill/tokens/preview/graphite-technical.css */ }
@theme inline {
  --color-base: var(--bg-base); --color-surface: var(--bg-surface); --color-sunken: var(--bg-sunken);
  --color-line: var(--border-default); --color-ink: var(--text-primary);
  --color-accent: var(--accent); --color-accent-hover: var(--accent-hover);
}
```

💡 If shadcn's `--background/--foreground` vars already exist, alias them to these — never carry two maps. `--color-*` aliases are optional sugar; recipes here use the raw vars.

## 2. Button — primary / secondary / ghost / danger

```tsx
const s = {
  base: "inline-flex h-9 select-none items-center justify-center gap-2 rounded-[var(--radius-md)] px-4 text-[length:var(--type-body)] font-medium transition-colors",
  states: "focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:[box-shadow:0_0_0_2px_var(--bg-base),0_0_0_4px_var(--accent)] active:bg-[var(--bg-active)] disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50",
  variants: {
    primary:   "bg-[var(--accent)] text-white hover:bg-[var(--accent-hover)] active:bg-[var(--accent-active)]",
    secondary: "border border-[var(--border-default)] text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:border-[var(--border-emphasis)] hover:bg-[var(--bg-hover)]",
    ghost:     "text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:bg-[var(--bg-hover)]",
    danger:    "border border-[var(--status-danger-border)] bg-[var(--status-danger-bg)] text-[var(--status-danger-text)] hover:brightness-110",
  },
};

export function Button({ variant = "secondary", className = "", ...props }) {
  return <button className={`${s.base} ${s.states} ${s.variants[variant]} ${className}`} {...props} />;
}
```

💡 Plain `<button>` keeps the kit dep-pure; compose as `<Slot>` when the app already ships `@radix-ui/react-slot`. `text-white` on primary is the one sanctioned literal — the accent is contrast-tuned per theme for ≥4.5:1 on it. 💡 Dangerous intent belongs to the danger variant + typed confirmation, never to a stylistic remix.

## 3. Input — sunken fill, halo focus, invalid state

```tsx
export function Input({ className = "", ...props }) {
  return (
    <input
      className={`h-9 w-full rounded-[var(--radius-md)] border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-sunken)] px-3 text-[length:var(--type-body)] text-[var(--text-primary)] placeholder:text-[var(--text-muted)] hover:border-[var(--border-emphasis)] focus-visible:outline-none focus-visible:border-[var(--accent)] focus-visible:ring-2 focus-visible:ring-[var(--accent)]/50 disabled:pointer-events-none disabled:opacity-50 aria-[invalid=true]:border-[var(--status-danger-border)] ${className}`}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}
```

Errors render as text below, wired with `aria-describedby`; the input carries only `aria-invalid` + the danger border.

## 4. Select / Tooltip / Badge / Card

```tsx
import * as SelectPrimitive from "@radix-ui/react-select";
import * as TooltipPrimitive from "@radix-ui/react-tooltip";

export function SelectTrigger({ className = "", ...props }) {
  return (
    <SelectPrimitive.Trigger
      className={`flex h-9 items-center justify-between gap-2 rounded-[var(--radius-md)] border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-sunken)] px-3 text-[length:var(--type-body)] text-[var(--text-primary)] hover:border-[var(--border-emphasis)] outline-none focus-visible:[box-shadow:0_0_0_2px_var(--bg-base),0_0_0_4px_var(--accent)] data-[state=open]:border-[var(--accent)] aria-[invalid=true]:border-[var(--status-danger-border)] ${className}`}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}

export function SelectContent({ className = "", children, ...props }) {
  return (
    <SelectPrimitive.Portal>
      <SelectPrimitive.Content position="popper" sideOffset={6}
        className={`z-20 max-h-72 min-w-[10rem] overflow-hidden rounded-[var(--radius-md)] border border-[var(--border-default)] bg-[var(--bg-elevated)] p-1 text-[length:var(--type-body)] text-[var(--text-primary)] [box-shadow:0_24px_48px_-12px_rgb(0_0_0/0.5)] ${className}`}
        {...props}>
        {children}
      </SelectPrimitive.Content>
    </SelectPrimitive.Portal>
  );
}

export function SelectItem({ className = "", children, ...props }) {
  return (
    <SelectPrimitive.Item
      className={`relative flex cursor-default select-none items-center rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] px-2 py-1.5 outline-none data-[highlighted]:bg-[var(--bg-hover)] data-[state=checked]:bg-[var(--accent-subtle)] ${className}`}
      {...props}
    />
  );
}

export function Tooltip({ children, label }) {
  return (
    <TooltipPrimitive.Root>
      <TooltipPrimitive.Trigger asChild>{children}</TooltipPrimitive.Trigger>
      <TooltipPrimitive.Portal>
        <TooltipPrimitive.Content sideOffset={6} className="z-30 rounded-[var(--radius-sm)] px-2.5 py-1.5 text-[length:var(--type-small)] bg-[oklch(0.92_0.005_265)] text-[oklch(0.20_0.01_265)] [box-shadow:0_4px_12px_rgb(0_0_0/0.25)]">
          {label}
        </TooltipPrimitive.Content>
      </TooltipPrimitive.Portal>
    </TooltipPrimitive.Root>
  );
}

export function Badge({ tone = "info", className = "", children }) {
  const tones = {
    info:    "bg-[var(--status-info-bg)] text-[var(--status-info-text)] border-[var(--status-info-border)]",
    success: "bg-[var(--status-success-bg)] text-[var(--status-success-text)] border-[var(--status-success-border)]",
    warning: "bg-[var(--status-warning-bg)] text-[var(--status-warning-text)] border-[var(--status-warning-border)]",
    danger:  "bg-[var(--status-danger-bg)] text-[var(--status-danger-text)] border-[var(--status-danger-border)]",
  };
  return (
    <span className={`inline-flex h-6 items-center rounded-[var(--radius-pill)] border px-2.5 text-[length:var(--type-small)] font-medium ${tones[tone]} ${className}`}>
      {children}
    </span>
  );
}

export function Card({ className = "", children, ...props }) {
  return <div className={`rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] p-4 ${className}`} {...props}>{children}</div>;
}
```

💡 Tooltip is the inversion rule: light fill + dark text even on dark pages. 💡 Badges are status-only — a pill without semantic reason is `pill-spam`. 💡 Floating panels keep a "top-edge light" (1px white/8% top border) + the single allowed ambient shadow (top layer only).

## 5. The 8-states CSS block (paste once per app)

```css
.di-interactive {
  background: var(--bg-surface); color: var(--text-primary);
  border: 1px solid var(--border-subtle);
  transition: background-color var(--motion-fast) var(--motion-enter),
              border-color var(--motion-fast) var(--motion-enter);
}
.di-interactive:hover:not(:disabled, [data-loading="true"]) { background: var(--bg-hover); border-color: var(--border-default); }
.di-interactive:focus-visible { outline: none; box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--bg-base), 0 0 0 4px var(--accent); }
.di-interactive:active:not(:disabled, [data-loading="true"]) { background: var(--bg-active); }
.di-interactive[aria-selected="true"], .di-interactive[data-state="selected"] { background: var(--accent-subtle); }
.di-interactive:disabled { opacity: 0.5; pointer-events: none; cursor: not-allowed; }
.di-interactive[data-loading="true"] { opacity: 0.7; pointer-events: none; }
.di-interactive[aria-invalid="true"], .di-interactive[data-state="error"] { border-color: var(--status-danger-border); }
.di-interactive .spinner {
  width: 1em; height: 1em; border-radius: var(--radius-pill); flex: none;
  border: 2px solid var(--border-default); border-top-color: var(--text-primary);
  animation: di-spin 600ms linear infinite;
}
@keyframes di-spin { to { transform: rotate(360deg); } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) {
  .di-interactive { transition-duration: 0s; }
  .di-interactive .spinner { animation: none; }
}
```

Spinner-in-button (loading state — `aria-busy` announced, no text tween):

```tsx
export function LoadingButton({ loading, children, ...props }) {
  return (
    <Button aria-busy={loading} data-loading={loading} disabled={loading} {...props}>
      {loading && <span className="spinner" aria-hidden="true" />}
      <span>{loading ? "Working…" : children}</span>
    </Button>
  );
}
```

💡 Selected ≠ hover: hover is the bg lift, selected is `--accent-subtle` (~12% alpha); on dark a flat accent-fill row is forbidden. Verify both themes with `../../checklists/dark-mode.md` and `../../checklists/a11y.md`.

# data-kit — React + Tailwind v4

Data surfaces: tables, stat tiles, charts, and the three honest non-ideal states. ✅ Assumes the core-kit token bridge (`--bg-*`, `--border-*`, `--text-*`, `--accent*`, `--status-*`, `--type-*`, `--radius-*`) exists in `globals.css` — no new deps (react + tailwind v4).

## 1. DataTable

```tsx
export function DataTable({ columns, rows, dense = false, empty = null }) {
  if (!rows.length) return empty ?? <EmptyState onAction={columns[0].newAction} />;
  return (
    <div className="max-h-[70vh] overflow-auto rounded-[var(--radius-md)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)]">
      <table className="di-table" data-density={dense ? "dense" : "comfortable"}>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            {columns.map((c) => (
              <th key={c.key} scope="col" className={c.numeric ? "num" : ""}>{c.label}</th>
            ))}
            <th scope="col"><span className="sr-only">Actions</span></th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {rows.map((row) => (
            <tr key={row.id} aria-selected={row.selected || undefined}>
              {columns.map((c) => <td key={c.key} className={c.numeric ? "num" : ""}>{row[c.key]}</td>)}
              <td className="actions">
                {row.actions.map((a) => <button key={a.label} className="di-ghost-icon" aria-label={a.label}>{a.icon}</button>)}
              </td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
  );
}
```

```css
.di-table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: var(--type-small); }
.di-table th {
  position: sticky; top: 0; z-index: 10; background: var(--bg-surface);
  border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-default);
  color: var(--text-secondary); font-weight: 500; text-align: left; white-space: nowrap;
}
.di-table th, .di-table td { height: 48px; padding: 0 12px; }
.di-table[data-density="dense"] th, .di-table[data-density="dense"] td { height: 40px; }
.di-table tbody tr { border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-subtle); transition: background-color var(--motion-fast) var(--motion-enter); }
.di-table tbody tr:hover { background: var(--bg-hover); }                 /* white/4–5% row lift in dark */
.di-table tbody tr[aria-selected="true"] { background: var(--accent-subtle); }
.di-table .num { text-align: right; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }  /* numerals right-aligned, tabular */
.di-table .actions { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; }
.di-ghost-icon {
  display: inline-flex; height: 28px; width: 28px; align-items: center; justify-content: center;
  border-radius: var(--radius-sm); color: var(--text-secondary);
}
.di-ghost-icon:hover { background: var(--bg-hover); color: var(--text-primary); }
.di-ghost-icon:focus-visible { outline: none; box-shadow: 0 0 0 2px var(--bg-base), 0 0 0 4px var(--accent); }
```

💡 Densities: 48px comfortable / 40px dense — announce the switch, keep one value per table. 💡 Mobile see `../../checklists/responsive.md`: financial tables keep horizontal scroll intent; defaults get a stacked-card fallback.

## 2. StatTile + sparkline SVG

```tsx
function Sparkline({ data, w = 96, h = 32 }) {
  const min = Math.min(...data), max = Math.max(...data);
  const pts = data.map((v, i) => [
    (i / (data.length - 1)) * (w - 3) + 1.5,
    h - 2 - ((v - min) / (max - min || 1)) * (h - 5),
  ]);
  const d = "M" + pts.map((p) => p.map((n) => n.toFixed(1)).join(" ")).join(" L");
  return (
    <svg width={w} height={h} viewBox={`0 0 ${w} ${h}`} className="block" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d={d} fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" strokeWidth="1.5" strokeLinecap="round" strokeLinejoin="round" />
    </svg>
  );
}

export function StatTile({ label, value, delta, trend }) {
  const up = delta >= 0;
  return (
    <Card>
      <div className="text-[length:var(--type-small)] text-[var(--text-secondary)]">{label}</div>
      <div className="mt-1 flex items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
        <span className="font-mono text-[26px] leading-none tracking-[-0.02em] text-[var(--text-primary)] tabular-nums">{value}</span>
        {trend?.length > 1 && <Sparkline data={trend} />}
      </div>
      <div className="mt-2 flex items-center gap-2">
        <Badge tone={up ? "success" : "danger"}>{up ? "▲" : "▼"} {Math.abs(delta)}%</Badge>
        <span className="text-[length:var(--type-small)] text-[var(--text-muted)]">vs last period</span>
      </div>
    </Card>
  );
}
```

💡 Value uses mono + tabular numerals; the delta badge is a status call, so it uses status tokens — accent stays out. Count-up animation only on login, ≤400ms, never ambient (fintech rule).

## 3. Chart color rules (dark) ✅

- Categorical hues: **≤7**, shifted toward cyan/magenta/yellow; hue steps ~15° inside the accent family for paired series.
- Gridlines/axes at white/6% → exactly `border-[var(--border-subtle)]`; axis text `var(--text-secondary)`.
- Monotone ramps run base → bright (never mid-saturated rainbow); sparklines 1.5px stroke.
- Legend on by default for >1 series; unit + timezone labels immutable; crosshair = `var(--border-emphasis)` line.
- Desaturate accent-heavy palettes −10–20% chroma vs light mode; red/green semantics always paired with shape/text.

## 4. Empty / Error / Loading states

```tsx
export function EmptyState({ title, hint, onAction, actionLabel = "Add first item" }) {
  return (
    <div className="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-3 rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border border-[var(--border-subtle)] bg-[var(--bg-surface)] py-16 text-center">
      <div className="flex h-12 w-12 items-center justify-center rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] bg-[var(--bg-sunken)] text-[var(--text-secondary)]">∅</div>
      <div>
        <div className="text-[length:var(--type-body)] font-medium text-[var(--text-primary)]">{title}</div>
        {hint && <p className="mt-1 max-w-sm text-[length:var(--type-small)] text-[var(--text-secondary)]">{hint}</p>}
      </div>
      <Button variant="primary" onClick={onAction}>{actionLabel}</Button>
    </div>
  );
}

export function ErrorState({ title = "Something went wrong", detail, onRetry }) {
  return (
    <div role="alert" className="flex flex-col items-center gap-3 rounded-[var(--radius-lg)] border border-[var(--status-danger-border)] bg-[var(--status-danger-bg)] py-12 text-center">
      <div className="text-[length:var(--type-body)] font-medium text-[var(--status-danger-text)]">{title}</div>
      {detail && <p className="max-w-md text-[length:var(--type-small)] text-[var(--text-secondary)]">{detail}</p>}
      <Button variant="secondary" onClick={onRetry}>Try again</Button>
    </div>
  );
}
```

Loading skeleton — for **>300ms** loads; pulse opacity only, never layout-reflow; layout identical to loaded content so IO is stable:

```css
.di-skeleton { border-radius: var(--radius-sm); background: var(--bg-hover); animation: di-pulse 1.4s linear infinite; }
@keyframes di-pulse { 0%, 100% { opacity: 1; } 50% { opacity: 0.55; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { .di-skeleton { animation: none; opacity: 0.55; } }
```

```tsx
export function TableSkeleton({ rows = 5, cols = 4 }) {
  return (
    <table className="di-table" aria-busy="true" aria-label="Loading content">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col" className="num" /><th scope="col" /><th scope="col" /><th scope="col" className="num" /></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        {Array.from({ length: rows }).map((_, r) => (
          <tr key={r}>
            {Array.from({ length: cols }).map((_, c) => (
              <td key={c}><span className="di-skeleton block h-3.5 w-20" style={{ width: (r + c) % 2 ? "5rem" : "8rem" }} /></td>
            ))}
          </tr>
        ))}
      </tbody>
    </table>
  );
}
```

💡 Spinners are only for <300ms or genuinely unknown duration; page-to-page buffers with skeletons, not spinners. Wrap results with the states from core-kit §5 (`data-loading`, `aria-invalid`, spinner).

# motion-kit — React + framer-motion + Tailwind v4

Orchestrated motion on the product's easing family: enter/exit, list stagger, a reduced-motion wrapper, and streaming text reveal for AI surfaces. ✅ Deps: `framer-motion` (only kit using it). Consistent with `skill/core/motion.md` budgets — one duration scale + one easing family per product.

## 1. Motion tokens (bridge)

```css
:root {
  --motion-fast: 80ms;   --motion-base: 160ms;  --motion-form: 240ms;
  --motion-enter: cubic-bezier(0.05, 0.7, 0.1, 1);   /* decelerate-out */
  --motion-exit:  cubic-bezier(0.3,  0,   1,   1);   /* fast-in */
}
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { * { transition-duration: 0.01ms !important; animation-duration: 0.01ms !important; } }
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: reduce) { *, *::before, *::after { scroll-behavior: auto !important; } }
```

Motion for React can't tween a CSS-var bezier from markup, so JS mirrors it once — keep the arrays identical to the tokens:

```tsx
const easeEnter = [0.05, 0.7, 0.1, 1] as const;  // = var(--motion-enter)
const easeExit  = [0.3, 0, 1, 1] as const;       // = var(--motion-exit)
```

## 2. Enter/exit (AnimatePresence)

Enter 160ms (`--motion-base`), exit 100ms ≈ 60–70% of enter. Exits never delay the next target.

```tsx
import { AnimatePresence, motion } from "framer-motion";

const pane = {
  initial: { opacity: 0, y: 8 },
  in:      { opacity: 1, y: 0,  transition: { duration: 0.16, ease: easeEnter } },
  out:     { opacity: 0, y: -6, transition: { duration: 0.10, ease: easeExit } },
};

export function RoutePane({ routeKey, children, className = "bg-[var(--bg-surface)] rounded-[var(--radius-lg)]" }) {
  return (
    <AnimatePresence mode="wait" initial={false}>
      <motion.div key={routeKey} variants={pane} initial="initial" animate="in" exit="out" className={className}>
        {children}
      </motion.div>
    </AnimatePresence>
  );
}
```

Springs are reserved for position/size (`type: "spring", stiffness: 260, damping: 26`); never spring color, text, or a layout-reflowing prop.

## 3. List stagger (≤30ms/item, capped at 160ms total)

```tsx
const listVariants = (n) => ({
  hidden: {},
  show: { transition: { staggerChildren: Math.min(0.03, 0.16 / Math.max(n - 1, 1)), delayChildren: 0 } },
});

const itemVariants = {
  hidden: { opacity: 0, y: 6 },
  show:   { opacity: 1, y: 0, transition: { duration: 0.16, ease: easeEnter } },
};

export function StaggerList({ items, renderItem }) {
  return (
    <motion.ul
      variants={listVariants(items.length)}
      initial="hidden" animate="show"
      className="flex flex-col divide-y divide-[var(--border-subtle)]"
    >
      {items.map((item) => (
        <motion.li key={item.id} variants={itemVariants} className="py-3">
          {renderItem(item)}
        </motion.li>
      ))}
    </motion.ul>
  );
}
```

💡 Cap exists so long lists don't accumulate delay chains (>600ms cumulative is the audit failure). First mount only — not on every render, not in table rows; entrances identical on every screen.

## 4. Reduced-motion wrapper → crossfade

`useReducedMotion` collapses moves into opacity-only swaps; instant (duration ≈ 0) per the global kill rule:

```tsx
import { useReducedMotion } from "framer-motion";

export function ReducedMotionPane({ routeKey, children }) {
  const reduced = useReducedMotion();
  const v = reduced
    ? { initial: { opacity: 0 }, animate: { opacity: 1 }, exit: { opacity: 0 } }
    : { initial: { opacity: 0, y: 8 }, animate: { opacity: 1, y: 0 }, exit: { opacity: 0, y: -6 } };
  return (
    <AnimatePresence mode="wait" initial={false}>
      <motion.div
        key={routeKey}
        initial={v.initial} animate={v.animate} exit={v.exit}
        transition={reduced ? { duration: 0.01 } : { duration: 0.16, ease: easeEnter }}
      >
        {children}
      </motion.div>
    </AnimatePresence>
  );
}
```

Reduced motion = crossfade only: opacity swaps at ~0 duration, exit included — no movement. Any component-level parallax/scroll effect must check `useReducedMotion` itself, not rely on this wrapper.

## 5. Streaming text chunk-reveal (AI products)

Linear stream — chunks append, no per-char tween; a line may settle cubic-out once at stream end. Chunks ≈ 50–80ms cadence:

```tsx
import { useEffect, useState } from "react";
import { useReducedMotion } from "framer-motion";

export function useStreamText(fullText, { chunk = 24, ms = 60 } = {}) {
  const reduced = useReducedMotion();
  const [text, setText] = useState("");
  useEffect(() => {
    if (reduced) { setText(fullText); return; }
    let i = 0; setText(fullText.slice(0, 0));
    const id = setInterval(() => {
      i = Math.min(i + chunk, fullText.length);
      setText(fullText.slice(0, i));
      if (i >= fullText.length) clearInterval(id);
    }, ms);
    return () => clearInterval(id);
  }, [fullText, chunk, ms, reduced]);
  return text;
}

export function StreamedAnswer({ fullText, streaming }) {
  const text = useStreamText(fullText);
  return (
    <div className="max-w-[68ch] text-[length:var(--type-body)] leading-[1.6] text-[var(--text-primary)]" aria-live="polite">
      {text}
      {streaming && <span aria-hidden="true" className="ml-0.5 inline-block h-4 w-[2px] translate-y-0.5 bg-[var(--text-secondary)]" />}
    </div>
  );
}
```

💡 Reduced motion renders the whole answer immediately (no interval). The caret is a 1-frame element, never an animated glow; the stream region is `aria-live="polite"` with a cancel/skip control nearby.

## 6. Budget guardrails ✅💡

- Per screen: ≤2 entrance animations, ≤3 simultaneous transitions, 0 ambient loops (AI waiting pulse is the sanctioned exception).
- Durations only from the scale `80 · 120 · 160 · 240 · 400 · 600`; keep it in one place, don't re-declare in components.
- Off-limits: parallax over body text, scroll-jacking, spinners >400ms, hover-lift+glow+tilt, padding-morph cards, entrance chains >600ms.
- Verify with `../../checklists/a11y.md` (reduced-motion honored, keyboard-operable controls) at 375/768/1440.
